 "problems": [
  "This batch owns no Cliopatria row; an earlier run (cut short, no report) had already written 11 dossiers (ba, shu, sanxingdui-culture, dian, xia-dynasty, yiqu, xianyu, wu-geng, dai-baidi, ju, xing); all validate and were kept unchanged, and are counted in dossiers_written with 'kept from an earlier run' in the name. 27 dossiers are new in this run. Wikidata ids are null throughout (unreachable).",
  "Nine of the new dossiers (jiang-zhengyang, jiang-gushi, liu-lu-an, eastern-guo, ji-shandong, sui-ningyang, yong-hubei, hu-luohe, kuai) rest on one verbatim row of the List of Zhou dynasty states (plus the Chu table row for four); they have no Wikipedia article of their own (identity.wikipedia null) and their starts marked '?' / 'Shang Era' / 'Xia Era' are bridges at 1046 (confidence 1). Regions are coordinates (the gazetteer lacks the places).",
  "Sibling dossiers need counterpart and region fixes to meet these: see history/polities/_notes/ea-01-x.md section 'Fixes the sibling dossiers need' (chu, jin, qi, qin, zheng, yan, zhou-dynasty, eastern-zhou, nanyue, han-dynasty). The most material: eastern-zhou's split should be 367 (not 314); qi lacks the Tan 684, Lai 567, Ji 690, Sui 681 gains; zheng's Hu, Hui and Eastern Guo gains can use the located discs; qin has no east-zhou vassal 307.",
  "Slug choices that depart from earlier suggestions: yong-hubei (yong is a Cliopatria row), liu-lu-an (not lu-2), qi-henan (not qi-2), ji-beijing (not ji-state), lai is Lai 萊 (Lai 賴 needs lai-2), jiang-zhengyang and jiang-gushi (not jiang / jiang-2), tan is Tan 譚 (Tan 郯 needs tan-state), kuai for the zheng dossier's 'Hui (鄶)'.",
  "Quanrong, Xianyun and Pi are people or legendary-origin dossiers drawn from a bridge year; family steppe for quanrong and xianyun (the colour agent may choose). xia-dynasty is type culture (group scope), a gap-filler may prefer dynasty.",
  "Jiang (state) and Yu (state) loaded as disambiguation pages; Yu has no article (red link). Warring States walls cannot be dossiers (no line object in the schema)."
 ]
